  "semantics": [
    "The wrapper processes exactly one channel. It loads filter-owner pointer, summary record pointer and state-owner pointer, ignores descriptor, then calls the channel update.",
    "The channel reads classification byte22, stores it at state+4, then reads summary flag byte41. Classification0 writes bool(flags) at state+5 while preserving state+6.",
    "Classification1 writes0 at state+5. Zero flags reset state+6; any nonzero byte increments it modulo256. Other classifications preserve bytes5/6.",
    "Volatile byte accesses preserve store-before-quality-load order and later counter loads, including overlap cases. No allocation, global state, assembly or opaque code is added.",
    "All S0-S31 and FPSCR are checked unchanged on direct tests, together with saved R4-R11, SP, interrupt masks and public RAM. Private stack bytes below incoming SP are excluded.",
    "Pipeline tests use actual C descriptor/aggregate/owned/filter-buffer constructors, heap, queues, ratio, summary and quality. Prior filter classification is an explicit input; the missing filter selector is not modeled or claimed implemented."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Relocatable composition with82 application and22 boot imports is not a complete bootable firmware image. Five SpO2 stages remain unresolved.",
    "Physical sensors, interrupt concurrency, hardware trap configuration and timing equivalence are untested. Unaligned owner cases use the emulator default unaligned-access behavior.",
    "Complete floating-point register checks cover S0-S31 and FPSCR, not separate FPU system/lazy-stacking configuration registers.",
    "Direct tests compare full public RAM except8192 bytes below incoming SP. Pipeline full RAM/FPSCR snapshots are at constructors and ratio/summary/quality/transition boundaries; per-push checks cover saved registers/SP only.",
    "Some preexisting transitive processing/math providers retain assembly; the new transition unit does not. All98 native body bytes execute, which does not establish exhaustive interleaving coverage.",
    "REA analysis snapshots are retained as evidence; locked raw firmware bytes execute for native replay."
  ],
